profiles: [low, high]
notes: >
  Parametric Student-t simulation model in agent/modeling.py — no learned
  artifacts, fully offline, self-calibrating per prompt from the 7-day minute
  context. EWMA variance (1d half-life) at the scored increment, full-strength
  median-based hour-of-day seasonality, mean reversion toward a robust 7-day
  target (median of per-day variances, 2d half-life), kurtosis-estimated
  Student-t df, GARCH-in-sim vol clustering (alpha 0.15, persistence 0.94),
  stratified quantile-grid serving with per-step permutation. Covers both
  formats: 24h/5-min (low: CRYPTO_24H, COM_EQU_24H) and 1h/1-min (high).
  Honors num_simulations (serves exactly what is requested; validator uses
  1000). Interface smoke-tested at 1000 sims on both formats: correct path
  count, time_length//time_increment+1 points per path, paths start at the
  last context price, values round-trip the validator's %.7e rule, ~0.3 s per
  prompt. Validation (validator-exact CRPS + ranking vs the offline field,
  1000 sims): W1 calm 24h weighted rank 49.5 (rank 1 on
  BTC/SOL/HYPE/XAU/NVDAX/GOOGLX), W2 high-vol 24h rank 121.8, W1 crypto-1h
  rank 49.3, W2 crypto-1h weighted rank 2.0 (rank 1 on BTC/ETH/SOL/HYPE),
  SP500 slice rank 77/138. See agent/report.md and agent/journal.md for the
  full campaign log.

  Unpacked with --allow-missing-data. modeling.py names artifacts/mlshape.pt at
  line 54 (ML_WEIGHTS, overridable via CAMPAIGN_ML_WEIGHTS) and that file was
  never committed: the ML shape model it belongs to was validated and DISCARDED
  in iteration 9 (regression dilution — see agent/journal.md), so what the tree
  carries is the validation checkpoint artifacts/mlshape_val.pt, not a
  production one. The branch that would load it is reached only when
  CAMPAIGN_ML_WEIGHTS' companion CAMPAIGN_INNOV is set to "ml"; the default is
  "studentt", and a torch.load failure there is caught and falls back to the
  parametric shape. So the served model is the parametric one described above,
  with or without the file — but note that nothing raises if it is missing.
